# tally 2.1.8 item 77 (item 8 of the follow-up): oa's sign test at pot depends on its day in window(04-05, 04-10), so
# the hole reaches oa's own flows (f1), and windows each splits them as the pin does (f2, f3). 2.1.8's first refcore
# printed 100.00 PLN. The review's b4_sign_ends.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place pot: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place jar: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wa: date
input db: date
input amt: money PLN

move oa: transfers
  on wa
  leg cash from pot to jar amount amt

move ob: transfers
  on db
  leg cash from world to pot amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wa = window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) "s"
  db = 2026-04-07 "s"
  opening[pot] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[jar] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask f1: flows(oa, 2026-04)
ask f2: flows(oa, 2026-04)
ask f3: flows(oa, 2026-04) with wa = 2026-04-05
=== expect
f1: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for flows of oa" (oa)
  unknown day: wa
  cut 2026-01-01
f2: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for flows of oa" (oa)
  unknown day: wa
  cut 2026-01-01
f3: refused: RUN-PLACE pot is -50.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-04-05
  pinned: wa = 2026-04-05
  cut 2026-01-01
